\tag{frap}
\title{Faces, flags, and the symmetry of a shape}

\p{An abstract polytope retains the incidence of vertices, edges and faces
without prescribing distances or angles. Schulte's flag formulation
\citet{Section 2}{schulte2017regular} leads from these incidences to
symmetries and to the extension of a facet symmetry used in
[local puzzle moves](frap-0009).}

